+## Voice enhancement demo
+
+The [offline Voice Isolator declaration](../../benchmarks/models/voice-isolator-v1.json)
+pins the released FP32 checkpoint. Place it at the declared path and use the
+public Inworld demo and golden clips declared in `voice-enhancement-demo-v1`.
+They are not samples from the private VIBE evaluation set.
+
+Compile the model with the [WebGPU guide](../../src/akas/models/voice_isolator/README.md),
+then run the upstream CPU and AKAS measurements serially:
+
+```sh
+uv run --no-sync python -m tools.baselines inworld voice-isolator-v1 --provider cpu --seconds 1800
+uv run --no-sync python -m tools.baselines akas voice-isolator-v1 --provider vulkan --bundle build/voice-isolator/f16 --reference-run UPSTREAM_CPU_RUN_ID --seconds 1800
+uv run --no-sync python -m tools.campaign_report --runs AKAS_RUN_ID --model voice-isolator-v1 --workload voice-enhancement-demo-v1
+```
+
+Both runtimes read identical WAVs with one warmup and three measured requests.
+The wall timer covers WAV decoding and complete offline enhancement, excluding
+model loading and WAV writing. It retains unnormalized FP32 voice/background
+pairs, deterministic hashes, golden and upstream numerical errors, and wall
+latency/RTF. F16 upload is selected by the compiled bundle and labeled
+separately from the original F32 checkpoint bytes and upstream F32 execution.
+No VIBE quality or accuracy score is claimed.
+
